<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Single source of truth for the version stamped into X1McpBridge.exe and X1McpGraphQL.exe.

  This number identifies a CONNECTOR RELEASE, and every binary in that release carries it -
  whichever flavor was built. The Lean flavor (the customer default) ships only X1McpBridge.exe and
  no net10 daemon at all, so "both exes always ship together" no longer holds; what still holds, and
  what matters, is that two binaries from the same release never report different versions, and two
  binaries reporting the same version are always from the same release. ProxyMode's relay-identity
  check and x1_version both depend on exactly that (see RelayHealth.Decide).

  Bump it with bump.bat rather than editing by hand - the exes must never disagree, and a
  hand-edit that touches only one of them reintroduces exactly the "which binary am I talking
  to" problem this version exists to answer.

  Do NOT add the build flavor here. This file is the version's single source of truth and bump.ps1
  regex-edits it; the flavor lives in build-installer.bat (X1MCP_FLAVOR), the daemon csproj's
  X1McpFlavor property, and build-info.json, and never enters this file.

  This is the connector's OWN build identity. It is deliberately NOT kept in sync with X1
  Search's version (x1buildversion-search.ini): the connector ships changes without an X1
  Search release, and reusing X1's number would give two different binaries the same version -
  destroying the identity the number exists to provide.
-->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <X1McpVersion>1.0.0.38</X1McpVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
